---

// Editorial page: fully static, rendered at build time.
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GameStage from '../components/GameStage.astro';
import { VERSIONS } from '../data/games';

const game = VERSIONS.find((v) => v.slug === 'parking-fury-3')!;

const videoGameSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'VideoGame',
  name: 'Parking Fury 3',
  description:
    'Third top-down parking game by Andriy Pidvirnyy, released on Coolmath Games on 19 October 2017 with the same WASD/arrow-key controls as its predecessors.',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Andriy Pidvirnyy' },
  datePublished: '2017-10-19',
  gamePlatform: 'Web browser',
  playMode: 'SinglePlayer',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  url: 'https://www.coolmathgames.com/0-parking-fury-3',
};
---

<BaseLayout jsonLd={[videoGameSchema]}>
  <header class="page-head container--wide">
    <span class="eyebrow">The series · entry three</span>
    <h1>Parking Fury 3: The Original Formula, Refined</h1>
    <p>
      Parking Fury 3 arrived on 19 October 2017, seven months after Parking Fury 2 and sixteen
      months after the original. Same developer — Andriy Pidvirnyy — same top-down view, same
      yellow parking space, same crash-means-retry rule. What you are really buying into is a
      fresh set of layouts.
    </p>
    <div class="chip-row">
      <span class="pill">Released 19 Oct 2017</span>
      <span class="pill">Andriy Pidvirnyy</span>
      <span class="pill">Browser + mobile</span>
      <span class="pill">Host: Coolmath Games</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section--tight container--wide" aria-label="Play Parking Fury 3">
    <GameStage
      title="Parking Fury 3"
      officialUrl={game.officialUrl}
      officialHost={game.host}
      embedUrl="https://www.bubbleshooter.net/embed.php?id=1697"
      miniGame={true}
      credit="Play Parking Fury 3 directly in your browser on this site."
    />
  </section>

  <section class="section container prose">
    <h2>What is actually new here</h2>
    <p>
      Not much — and that is the point. Coolmath’s own FAQ describes the sequels as playing
      “very similarly to the first Parking Fury, just with new maps and a couple of new
      features.” Parking Fury 3 keeps the instruction sheet of its predecessors verbatim: use
      WASD or the arrow keys, follow the arrows, stop in the yellow parking space, and avoid
      walls and parked cars.
    </p>
    <p>
      The official page files it under <strong>Skill → Hard Controls</strong> and lists planning
      as the skill it trains — a slightly slimmer list than Parking Fury 2, which also credits
      visual-spatial reasoning and estimation. Coolmath publishes no level count for this entry,
      so treat any specific number from other sites as unverified.
    </p>

    <div class="note">
      <span aria-hidden="true">ℹ</span>
      <span>
        <strong>Series lineup (all on Coolmath Games):</strong> Parking Fury (26 May 2016),
        Parking Fury 2 (23 March 2017), Parking Fury 3 (19 October 2017) — all by Andriy
        Pidvirnyy. The 3D games are a separate series by a different studio.
      </span>
    </div>

    <h2>Controls are unchanged across the trilogy</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data">
        <caption>Official instructions, checked October 2026</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Action</th>
            <th scope="col">Keyboard</th>
            <th scope="col">Touch</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Accelerate</th>
            <td><kbd class="kbd">W</kbd> / <kbd class="kbd">↑</kbd></td>
            <td>Gas pedal</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Reverse</th>
            <td><kbd class="kbd">S</kbd> / <kbd class="kbd">↓</kbd></td>
            <td>Brake pedal</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Steer</th>
            <td><kbd class="kbd">A</kbd><kbd class="kbd">D</kbd> / <kbd class="kbd">←</kbd><kbd class="kbd">→</kbd></td>
            <td>Rotate the on-screen wheel</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Objective</th>
            <td colspan="2">Follow the arrows and stop inside the yellow rectangle without hitting anything</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      More detail — including what differs in the 3D games — is on the
      <a href="/how-to-play/">controls page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How to get through it</h2>
    <p>
      The layouts are the only variable, so the method that works on level 1 of the original
      works here: finish your braking in a straight line, cut a wide entry angle, and crawl into
      the bay. Our <a href="/walkthrough/">walkthrough page</a> covers the structure of the
      series and the late-game difficulty spike, and <a href="/tips/">the tips page</a> lists the
      four mistakes that cause most restarts.
    </p>

    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href={game.officialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Play Parking Fury 3 on Coolmath Games<span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
      </a>
      <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/parking-fury-2/">Previous: Parking Fury 2</a>
    </div>

    <h2>More from the series</h2>
    <ul class="link-list">
      <li>
        <a class="link-card" href="/">
          <span class="link-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <span><strong>Parking Fury (2016)</strong><span>The original — guide, controls and our original mini-game, Tight Lot.</span></span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="link-card" href="/parking-fury-2/">
          <span class="link-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <span><strong>Parking Fury 2 (2017)</strong><span>The middle entry, with the official skills list published for it.</span></span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="link-card" href="/parking-fury-3d/">
          <span class="link-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">3D</span>
          <span><strong>Parking Fury 3D</strong><span>Same brand name, different developer — a 3D game on Poki.</span></span>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
